				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				105,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Install Wind workbench bridge after services ready\n\nAdd an event-driven installation path for Wind's LandWorkbench bridge that listens for the `cel:services-ready` event dispatched by Output's `ExposeWorkbenchAccessor` transform. Once services are available, `InstallLandWorkbench()` is dynamically imported and executed, which in turn dispatches `cel:wind-ready` for downstream subscribers (SkyBridge, Astro components, in-page Wind tasks).\n\nThis change ensures proper sequencing: services DI container populated → install Wind bridge → notify subscribers. The entire block is guarded by `if (!LandDisabled)` so bisect mode (`Disable=true`) keeps the workbench probe-free as intended in the recent Disable=true feature.\n\nRefs: IT-01 from `.claude/workflow/05-Open-Threads.md`",
			"SHA": "8c65df03c7c282ed629ec43a2a29947d3f08334d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T01:17:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				105,
				1
			],
			"Message": "perf(Sky): Batch command registration to reduce IPC channel saturation\n\nThe `sky://command/register` handler now accepts either a single command object (legacy shape) or a batch `{ commands: [...] }` object. Mountain's extension boot path registers 100+ extensions, each with ~10 commands = 1000+ individual emit events. This saturated Tauri's shared WKWebView IPC channel, queuing keystrokes behind thousands of register events.\n\nThe new batch format processes all commands in a single IPC round-trip via the new `RegisterOneCommand` helper, dramatically reducing channel traffic and restoring keystroke responsiveness during extension boot.",
			"SHA": "06fd1942a6b149f4e55cf0c0eca1ad4894d709b5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T00:15:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				105,
				1
			],
			"Message": "perf(Sky): Reduce IPC channel saturation by making diagnostic logging opt-in\n\nRemove per-fire diagnostic traces and replace with failure-only logging or opt-in flags. The original RenderDevLog calls for textSearch, fileSearch, and TreeView attach fired on every invocation (50-100/s during extension boot), doubling traffic on Tauri's single serialized WKWebView channel and starving keystroke delivery.\n\n_CelDispatchLog now requires globalThis.__LAND_TRACE_CEL_DISPATCH__=true. Diagnostic bridges for markers-bridge and webview-bridge now only log when pushable=false or hasRegister=false, capturing the triage value without saturating the channel on the success path.\n\nKeystroke delivery should be more responsive during extension boot.",
			"SHA": "131245270726f95b174ac9a9ac9c98a9e50583ce"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T23:44:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				105,
				2
			],
			"Message": "Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Sky into Current",
			"SHA": "83a7b8975aa291f68d89c3e212b4a8e13ff21ddf"
		}
